 Contacts currently live only in the page session. Preserve the existing list and
 keep the result runnable locally; no external service is needed. A typical input
 is in `example.csv`.
+
+## CSV import
+
+Click **导入 CSV** and pick a file. The first row must be a header containing
+`姓名` and `邮箱` (`名字` / `name` / `email` work too); `公司` is optional.
+Imported contacts are appended to the existing list, and duplicates are matched
+by email — so importing the same file twice adds nothing.
+
+Encoding is detected from the bytes, so UTF-8 (with or without BOM), UTF-16 with a
+BOM, and the GB18030 files saved by Chinese Excel are all read correctly. Quoted
+fields, doubled quotes (`""`) and line breaks inside quotes parse per RFC 4180.
+
+Unusable rows are skipped with a reason and their line number. A file with a
+missing required column, an unclosed quote, or no content is rejected outright and
+the list is left untouched. Imported contacts last for the page session only —
+reloading restores the built-in list.
